00:56:09,473 --> 00:56:15,473
The Criminal (released in the United States as The Concrete Jungle) is a 1960 British neo-noir crime film directed by
Joseph Losey and starring Stanley Baker, Sam Wanamaker, Grégoire Aslan, Jill Bennett, and Margit Saad.

12
01:01:15,789 --> 01:01:21,789
Baker plays Johnny Bannion, a recently paroled gangster (patterned after Albert Dimes) who is sent back to prison
after robbing a racetrack, with both the authorities and the criminal underworld looking for the money.

13
01:06:22,105 --> 01:06:28,105
Alun Owen wrote the screenplay, from a story by an uncredited Jimmy Sangster.

14
01:11:28,421 --> 01:11:34,421
John Dankworth composed the musical score, with a title song sung by Cleo Laine.

15
01:16:34,736 --> 01:16:40,736
The ensemble supporting cast features Jill Bennett, Rupert Davies, Laurence
Naismith, Patrick Magee and Murray Melvin in his film debut.

16
01:21:41,052 --> 01:21:47,052
The film, a  “B” melodrama  is noted for its harsh and violent portrayal of prison life
which led it to be banned in several countries, including Finland and Ireland.

17
01:26:47,368 --> 01:26:53,368
The film explores themes of robbery, b movie, racetrack, british noir.

18
01:31:53,684 --> 01:31:59,684
The tone is dark.
